00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.928
What's inside AI training data?
Your words? A benchmark's exam questions?

00:00:04.928 --> 00:00:08.533
Until now, every answer was a score.
A percentage. Trust us.

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:11.221
Ingot answers differently.
It shows you the words.

00:00:11.221 --> 00:00:16.119
Drop a training corpus. The scan runs —
and every overlap is shown word for word.

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:20.352
Like this exam question, found inside
twenty-one gigabytes of web text.

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:24.981
And what leaves your machine? Zero bytes.
Not a policy — your browser enforces it.

00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:26.932
Nine million documents scanned.

00:00:26.932 --> 00:00:32.661
Every published number gated in CI — and every
report ends with a receipt anyone can re-run.

00:00:32.661 --> 00:00:35.306
Ask it yourself — in your browser,
or one command.
